# ─── Outside datasets/, everything is published ──────────────────────────────
# All source, firmware, documents, the paper and its figures are tracked. The only
# things excluded here are GENERATED or MACHINE-LOCAL: they are not authored content
# and would be rebuilt or rewritten on any other machine.
build/
build-*/
.cache/
# .venv is 627 MB and self-excludes via a .gitignore inside itself, which is too
# fragile a thing to rely on for an accident that size. Listed here explicitly.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.log
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
.codex/
diagnostics/
# imgui.ini is the runtime window layout, rewritten every run.
# vbt_config.json is local configuration and carries machine-specific paths.
imgui.ini
vbt_config.json

# The paper is NOT published. paper/ holds the manuscript, its sources
# (PAPER_SOURCE.md, PROMPT.md), the .tex sections, references.bib and the figures.
# It stays local. Note that README.md and docs/ link into it: those links resolve in
# a local clone and will not resolve on the remote, which is stated where they appear.
paper/

# ─── Inside datasets/ ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THE MEASUREMENT IS NOT PUBLISHED. camera/ (marker positions, infrared video) and
# imu/ (the raw streams) are ~7.6 GB and stay outside the repository, as does
# smoothed.csv, the per-frame reference track. What IS published, per session, is the
# ANNOTATION, the METADATA and the AUDITS; and at the datasets/ root, the ground
# truth and the corpus documents.
#
# Written as: ignore everything, then re-admit by name. The two directory
# re-admissions (!datasets/session_*/) are required — an ignored directory is not
# descended into, so a rule inside it would never be reached.
datasets/*
datasets/session_*/*

# the ground truth and the corpus documents
!datasets/ground_truth.csv
!datasets/README.md
!datasets/REVIEW.md
!datasets/KNOWN_LIMITATIONS.md
!datasets/*.png

# the session folders themselves, so the rules below are reachable
!datasets/session_*/

# the annotation: as recorded live, the same algorithm re-run on the corrected
# track, rules 1-6, and the reviewer's accept/reject
!datasets/session_*/annotation_*.csv

# the metadata: what describes the session rather than measures it
!datasets/session_*/metadata.json
!datasets/session_*/manifest.json
!datasets/session_*/rotation.json
!datasets/session_*/sync_map.csv
!datasets/session_*/events.jsonl
!datasets/session_*/CHECKSUMS.sha256

# the audits: the reference annotation, the inertial comparison, and the
# camera-free pipeline under each attitude engine
!datasets/session_*/audit_*.png
